
2018: Direct installation from Github
	To get the latest version using git (in subfolder "MPSolve") do:
		> git clone git://github.com/robol/MPSolve.git
		> cd MPSolve
		> [...use apt-cyg to install autoconf, automake, libtool]
		> ./autogen.sh
		> ./configure
		> [found that I did not have "doxygen", so install with apt-cyg]
	<<<-----------------------------------------------
MPSolve configuration:
        Source location:        .
        Pthread CFLAGS:
        C compiler:             gcc
        CFLAGS:                 -D_REENTRANT -Wall -DMPS_USE_BUILTIN_COMPLEX  -DNICE_DEBUG -fcx-limited-range -fno-math-errno -fomit-frame-pointer -D_MPS_PRIVATE
        LDFLAGS:                  -mwindows -no-undefined -Wl,--export-all-symbols -Wl,--output-def,.libs/libmps-3.dll.def
        Additional CFLAGS:      -g -O2 -D__WINDOWS
        Debug enabled:          yes
        Check enabled:          yes
        Octave module:          no
        MATLAB (tm) module:     no
        Graphical UI:           no
        Python module:          no
	>>>-----------------------------------------------
		> make
	<<<-----------------------------------------------
	ERROR 2 -- did not have YACC.
	So I installed the Berkeley yacc ("byacc") (since there is no "yacc")
	But would not work?
	make failed again, and so I re-do ./configure again.
	This time, "make" found and used "byacc"!
	BUT, get LOTS of "warning: implicit declaration of function '_fileno' "
		REASON: If you did not pre-declare a function XXX before first
		use of XXX, it will assume that XXX returns an int.  
		Apparently, if we use C11 or newer compilers, this would go
		away.
	Finally, ERROR 2 again -- seems to be because I am missing "flex"
	although flex seem to only cause a "warning"...
	So, here we go again:
	>>>-----------------------------------------------
		> apt-cyg install byacc
		> apt-cyg install flex
		> ./configure
		> make (AGAIN)
	<<<-----------------------------------------------
	All the "warning: implicit declaration of function '_fileno' "
	remains.  Still error!!!  So we never got to the next step
	which is to "make install":
	>>>-----------------------------------------------
		> [sudo] make install
	<<<-----------------------------------------------
	>>>-----------------------------------------------
	
